{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch8axrs6V3sbPtvt5vxA5", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "1. **Reports (last 6 h):** There is one report. A wheelchair user said at 13:25 UTC today (about 6 minutes old) that they had just seen the lift out of service. It is lift ASC.PMR 4556 ASC3, serving platforms 50/51 (north underpass) at Juvisy (SNCF).\n2. **Contradiction:** The report contradicts the official status. SNCF's hourly feed shows AVAILABLE, last updated 09:30 UTC. IDFM's lift dataset shows UNAVAILABLE, updated 2026-11-16 03:39, so the two official sources disagree with each other.\n3. **Check first:** Inspect Juvisy ASC3 on platforms 50/51 now. The rider report and the IDFM status both point to a fault, and the SNCF \"available\" status is about 4 hours old.\n4. **Follow-up:** If the lift is confirmed out, correct the SNCF status and the passenger information. If it is working, find out why IDFM has shown it as down since yesterday. The report is unverified and doesn't change the official status."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 863, "cache_read_input_tokens": 25686, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 863}, "output_tokens": 360, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "969562bd-6881-45c6-8de3-18fb5ac915f4", "uuid": "f59b5151-8a67-423c-aa8e-ccd675ea2cef", "timestamp": "2026-11-17T13:33:56.273Z", "request_id": "req_011Ch8axrby4K95uUKpJevFg"}
